Data definition: CREATE, ALTER, DROP
CREATE DATABASE shop;
USE shop;
SHOW TABLES;

CREATE TABLE ITEM (
    ItemNo   INT PRIMARY KEY,
    IName    VARCHAR(25) NOT NULL,
    Category VARCHAR(15),
    Price    FLOAT,
    Qty      INT DEFAULT 0
);
DESCRIBE ITEM;

ALTER TABLE ITEM ADD Supplier VARCHAR(20);   -- add a column
ALTER TABLE ITEM DROP Supplier;              -- remove a column
ALTER TABLE ITEM MODIFY IName VARCHAR(40);   -- change a column's type/size
DROP TABLE ITEM;                             -- delete the table completely

Data manipulation: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
INSERT INTO ITEM VALUES (1, 'Pen', 'Stationery', 10, 200);
INSERT INTO ITEM (ItemNo, IName, Price) VALUES (2, 'Mouse', 499);

UPDATE ITEM SET Price = Price * 1.10 WHERE Category = 'Stationery';
UPDATE ITEM SET Qty = 50 WHERE ItemNo = 2;

DELETE FROM ITEM WHERE Qty = 0;

Careful: UPDATE and DELETE without a WHERE clause affect every row in the table.

Data query: SELECT … FROM … WHERE
SELECT reads data from a table. Use `*` for all columns, or name the columns you want, separated by commas.

SELECT * FROM ITEM;
SELECT IName, Price FROM ITEM;
SELECT ItemNo, IName, Category FROM ITEM;

Add a WHERE clause to filter rows using a relational operator: `=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`, `<>` (not equal to).

SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE Category = 'Stationery';
SELECT IName, Price FROM ITEM WHERE Price > 100;
SELECT IName, Qty FROM ITEM WHERE Qty <= 10;
SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE Category <> 'Electronics';

Combine more than one condition with the logical operators AND, OR and NOT. AND needs both conditions true; OR needs at least one true; NOT reverses a condition.

SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE Price > 100 AND Category = 'Electronics';
SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE Category = 'Stationery' OR Category = 'Books';
SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE NOT Category = 'Electronics';
SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE Qty > 0 AND Price < 500;

BETWEEN … AND … tests whether a value lies in a range, with both ends included.

SELECT * FROM ITEM WHERE Price BETWEEN 50 AND 500;
SELECT IName, Qty FROM ITEM WHERE Qty BETWEEN 10 AND 100;
SELECT RNo, Name, DOB FROM STUDENT WHERE DOB BETWEEN '2008-01-01' AND '2008-12-31';

NULL means a missing or unknown value — it is not the same as zero or blank text. Test it with IS NULL / IS NOT NULL, never with `= NULL`.

SELECT IName FROM ITEM WHERE Supplier IS NULL;
SELECT IName, Category FROM ITEM WHERE Category IS NOT NULL;
SELECT RNo, Name FROM STUDENT WHERE Marks IS NULL;

Clause/Operator | Purpose
WHERE | Filter rows by a condition
= , < , > , <= , >= , <> | Compare a column's value (relational operators)
AND / OR / NOT | Combine or reverse conditions
BETWEEN … AND … | Match a range of values (inclusive)
IS NULL / IS NOT NULL | Find rows where a value is missing / not missing
